{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":117748,"duration_api_ms":115971,"num_turns":16,"result":"Perfect! I have successfully analyzed the 1000 Genomes workflow and generated the knowledge report. Here is the complete file content:\n\n---\n\n# 1000Genome Workflow Knowledge Report\n\n**Workflow Name:** 1000genome\n**Analysis Agent:** Claude\n**Analysis Date:** 2026-03-11\n**Analysis Type:** Static code analysis (no deployment/runtime evaluation)\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe 1000 Genomes workflow is a scientific bioinformatics pipeline that analyzes human genetic variation from the 1000 Genomes Project. It identifies mutational overlaps between individuals by:\n1. Parsing per-chromosome VCF (variant call format) files to extract individual genotypes\n2. Filtering variants by predicted functional impact (SIFT scores)\n3. Cross-matching mutations between pairs of individuals\n4. Computing frequency distributions of mutation overlaps across random individual samples\n\nThe workflow uses the Pegasus WMS for orchestration and exhibits a **per-chromosome fan-in/fan-out parallel structure** with secondary parallelism across multiple populations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Stages and Tasks\n\n### Stage 1: Data Parsing (Per-Chromosome Parallelism)\n\n#### Task: `individuals`\n- **Executable:** `bin/individuals.py` (or bash equivalent `bin/individuals`)\n- **Type:** Data extraction and filtering\n- **Per-Chromosome Scaling:** For each chromosome, multiple `individuals` tasks may execute in parallel if `--individuals-jobs` > 1\n- **Inputs:**\n  - VCF file: `ALL.chrX.250000.vcf` (one per chromosome, ~250k lines each)\n  - Metadata: `columns.txt` (sample identifiers, ~2504 individuals)\n- **Outputs:**\n  - Per-individual mutation archives: `chrXn-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` (one per job chunk)\n  - Each archive contains per-individual files named `chrX.{individual_id}` with filtered mutation data\n- **Processing:**\n  - Reads VCF file in line ranges (e.g., lines 1-50k, 50k-100k) to enable parallel processing\n  - Filters to allele frequency (AF) ≥ 0.5 OR AF < 0.5 based on genotype\n  - For each of 2504 individuals, writes one output file listing their mutations\n  - Compresses individual files into tarball for staging efficiency\n- **Parallelization Parameter:** `ind_jobs` (1 to N per chromosome; default=1, max=250)\n\n#### Task: `individuals_merge`\n- **Executable:** `bin/individuals_merge.py` (or bash `bin/individuals_merge`)\n- **Type:** Consolidation/merge\n- **Trigger:** Depends on all `individuals` tasks for a given chromosome\n- **Inputs:**\n  - All `chrXn-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` archives from `individuals` tasks for chromosome X\n- **Outputs:**\n  - Merged archive: `chrXn.tar.gz` (one per chromosome)\n  - Contains consolidated per-individual files for the entire chromosome\n- **Processing:**\n  - Extracts and merges individual mutation files across all job chunks\n  - Concatenates per-individual data to restore full per-chromosome view\n  - Re-compresses into single archive per chromosome\n\n### Stage 2: Variant Effect Annotation (Per-Chromosome Parallelism)\n\n#### Task: `sifting`\n- **Executable:** `bin/sifting.py` (or bash `bin/sifting`)\n- **Type:** Variant annotation/filtering\n- **Inputs:**\n  - VEP annotation file: `ALL.chrX.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` (per chromosome)\n- **Outputs:**\n  - SIFT scores file: `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt` (one per chromosome)\n  - Format: `line_number rs_id ENSG_id SIFT_score phenotype`\n- **Processing:**\n  - Filters VEP annotation file for variants with SIFT predictions\n  - Extracts rs numbers (variant identifiers), ENSEMBL gene IDs, SIFT scores, and phenotype predictions\n  - Drops variants lacking SIFT annotation\n- **Parallelization:** One task per chromosome (can run in parallel with `individuals` + `individuals_merge`)\n\n### Stage 3: Analysis (Per-Population Parallelism)\n\n#### Task: `mutation_overlap`\n- **Executable:** `bin/mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Type:** Cross-individual analysis\n- **Arguments:** `-c {chromosome} -pop {population}`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - Merged individuals archive: `chrXn.tar.gz`\n  - SIFT scores file: `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt`\n  - Population file: `{population}` (from `data/populations/`)\n  - Metadata: `columns.txt`\n- **Outputs:**\n  - Analysis results archive: `chrX-{population}.tar.gz` (stage_out=True)\n  - Contains:\n    - Overlap statistics (pair-wise intersection counts)\n    - Visualization plots (colormap, histograms as `.png` files)\n    - Organized in subdirectories: `output_no_sift/`, `plots_no_sift/`\n- **Processing:**\n  - Reads individual mutation files and SIFT-filtered variant list\n  - For each population, identifies individuals in that population\n  - Computes pair-wise intersection counts (how many mutations overlap between any two individuals)\n  - Generates visualizations (heatmaps, histograms) of mutation overlap patterns\n- **Parallelization:** Runs once per chromosome × population combination (e.g., 22 chr × 7 populations = 154 tasks)\n\n#### Task: `frequency`\n- **Executable:** `bin/frequency.py`\n- **Type:** Statistical sampling analysis\n- **Arguments:** `-c {chromosome} -pop {population}`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - Merged individuals archive: `chrXn.tar.gz`\n  - SIFT scores file: `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt`\n  - Population file: `{population}`\n  - Metadata: `columns.txt`\n- **Outputs:**\n  - Frequency results archive: `chrX-{population}-freq.tar.gz` (stage_out=True)\n  - Contains:\n    - Mutation overlap frequency distributions (1000 random samples)\n    - Visualization plots (distribution histograms as `.png` files)\n- **Processing:**\n  - Reads same inputs as `mutation_overlap`\n  - Samples N_indiv=52 individuals randomly (1000 iterations)\n  - For each random sample, counts overlapping mutations using multiset intersection\n  - Generates frequency histogram showing how often specific overlap counts occur\n  - Provides null distribution for statistical testing\n- **Parallelization:** Runs once per chromosome × population combination (same cardinality as `mutation_overlap`)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Objects Registry\n\n### Input Data Objects\n\n| Name | Format | Size Estimate | Source | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------------|--------|---------|\n| `ALL.chrX.250000.vcf` | Text (VCF) | ~100-500 MB | `data/{dataset}/` | Per-chromosome genotype data (Phase3, 2504 individuals) |\n| `ALL.chrX.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` | Text (VEP) | ~50-200 MB | `data/{dataset}/sifting/` | Per-chromosome variant effect predictions |\n| `columns.txt` | Text (TSV) | ~50 KB | `data/{dataset}/` | Individual sample IDs and metadata (~2504 individuals) |\n| `{population}` | Text (list) | ~1-5 KB | `data/populations/` | Newline-separated individual IDs for specific population (AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) |\n\n### Intermediate Data Objects\n\n| Name | Format | Source Task | Consumed By | Purpose |\n|------|--------|-------------|-------------|---------|\n| `chrXn-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` | Tarball (gzip) | `individuals` | `individuals_merge` | Per-job per-individual mutation files (intermediate, not staged out) |\n| `chrXn.tar.gz` | Tarball (gzip) | `individuals_merge` | `mutation_overlap`, `frequency` | Consolidated per-individual mutation files for chromosome (intermediate, not staged out) |\n| `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt` | Text (TSV) | `sifting` | `mutation_overlap`, `frequency` | SIFT-annotated variant list per chromosome (intermediate, not staged out) |\n\n### Output Data Objects\n\n| Name | Format | Source Task | Staging | Purpose |\n|------|--------|-------------|---------|---------|\n| `chrX-{population}.tar.gz` | Tarball (gzip) | `mutation_overlap` | Yes (stage_out=True) | Pair-wise mutation overlap statistics and heatmap plots |\n| `chrX-{population}-freq.tar.gz` | Tarball (gzip) | `frequency` | Yes (stage_out=True) | Frequency distribution and histogram plots |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Producer-Consumer Dependencies\n\nThe workflow follows a per-chromosome fan-in/fan-out pattern with secondary per-population parallelism:\n\n- **Individuals parsing** and **sifting** run independently per chromosome\n- **Individuals_merge** consolidates all individual job chunks per chromosome\n- **Mutation_overlap** and **frequency** depend on merged individuals and SIFT scores, running once per chromosome-population pair\n\nAll cross-chromosome and cross-population dependencies are absent, enabling embarrassingly parallel execution.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Workflow-Level Pattern\n\n### Structural Classification: **Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with Multi-Level Parallelism**\n\n**Pattern:** Per-chromosome fan-in/fan-out with secondary per-population parallelism.\n\n**Topology:**\n- Chromosomes 1–22 processed independently (no cross-chromosome data flow)\n- Per chromosome: `individuals` splits into N parallel jobs → `individuals_merge` consolidation\n- Per chromosome: `sifting` runs independently in parallel\n- Per chromosome-population pair: `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` analysis tasks\n- 7 populations (AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) create secondary parallelism\n- No conditional branching; deterministic task cardinality\n\n---\n\n## 5. I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n### Key I/O Characteristics\n\n1. **Tarball-Based Intermediate Staging:**\n   - Per-individual mutation files bundled into compressed archives to reduce staging overhead\n   - `individuals` → `chrXn-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` → `individuals_merge` → `chrXn.tar.gz`\n\n2. **Per-Individual File Proliferation:**\n   - ~2504 individual files created per chromosome split\n   - Compressed into single archive per job for efficient transfer\n\n3. **Small Metadata Fan-Out:**\n   - `columns.txt` and population files replicated to every analysis task\n   - Size negligible (~1-5 KB); minimal staging impact\n\n4. **Repeated Tarball Extraction:**\n   - Both `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` independently extract `chrXn.tar.gz`\n   - Redundant extraction if co-scheduled; potential optimization with shared filesystem\n\n5. **Memory Scaling with Data Size:**\n   - Per-task memory scales with VCF line count per chunk\n   - README reports: 2.93 GB (16 splits) to 6.10 GB (2 splits) for 250k-line input\n\n---\n\n## 6. Summary of Key Insights\n\n### Workflow Structure\n- **High Parallelism:** Per-chromosome (22) × per-population (7) × per-job splits (1-N) = up to 154+ independent tasks\n- **Merge Pattern:** Consolidates split jobs while maintaining per-chromosome consistency\n- **Stateless Analysis:** Each analysis task operates independently without side effects\n\n### Data Flow\n- **Compression Strategy:** Tarball wrapping optimizes intermediate staging\n- **Format Transformation:** VCF (variant × individual) → per-individual text files\n- **Filtering Stages:** Allele frequency (individuals), SIFT annotation (sifting), population membership (analysis tasks)\n\n### Performance Observations (from README)\n- **Dominant Task:** `individuals` comprises 81.85% of execution time\n- **Memory Scaling:** Critical parameter for resource-constrained environments\n- **Clustering Options:** Decaf or MPI clustering available to reduce overhead\n\n---\n\nSTATUS: success | OUTPUT: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial3.md","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c6789fc6-6975-4eeb-82d0-b3e0ab494d4a","total_cost_usd":0.17300845,"usage":{"input_tokens":130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41005,"cache_read_input_tokens":642222,"output_tokens":11480,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41005,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":130,"outputTokens":11480,"cacheReadInputTokens":642222,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41005,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.17